08:17.320 --> 08:23.580
a proprietary Qualcomm header format which is a 40 byte header that dictates where in memory

08:23.580 --> 08:29.080
certain sections of trust zone are loaded which is fairly easy to sort of guess the meaning of

08:29.080 --> 08:32.740
and I think some people have gone out of their way to provide third party documentation on

08:32.740 --> 08:38.000
that. But nowadays the more recent trust zone kernels are actually ELF binaries so you can

08:38.000 --> 08:43.000
load them up in IDA pro and it will handle loading things in memory for you and then you can go to

08:43.000 --> 08:50.000
work. Now I find it's a useful exercise whenever beginning any sort of vulnerability research

08:50.660 --> 08:55.660
