11:34.820 --> 11:39.620
no remote attack surface for most real trust zone implementations. It's very difficult to

11:39.620 --> 11:45.120
imagine a sane use case where the trust zone kernel on a phone needs to receive data directly

11:45.120 --> 11:51.320
remotely. That having been said we also want to assume that the attacker has kernel privileges

11:51.320 --> 11:56.420
